{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0152VwWf8VFWapbiT9fLCNtV","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 3 Implementation: Planner Artifact Inheritance\n2\t\n3\t**Status**: Complete ✓\n4\t**Date**: 2026-07-24\n5\t**Scope**: Implementation of planner decision methods to examine prior worker artifacts and populate inherited_artifacts in spawn requests.\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## Summary\n10\t\n11\tPhase 3 successfully implements planner-side artifact inheritance. The planner now:\n12\t\n13\t1. **Examines prior worker produced_artifacts** — Collects artifacts from the most recent completed worker before creating new spawn requests\n14\t2. **Populates inherited_artifacts in SpawnRequests** — Passes discovered artifacts to the next worker via the spawn request\n15\t3. **Records artifact inheritance chain** — Maintains audit trail of which worker produced which artifacts\n16\t4. **Includes reasoning for inheritance** — Artifact inheritance logic is traceable and auditable\n17\t\n18\tAll changes are backward compatible. Existing workflows without produced_artifacts declarations continue to work without modification.\n19\t\n20\t---\n21\t\n22\t## Changes Implemented\n23\t\n24\t### 1. Turn Module (app/services/orchestrator/turn.rb)\n25\t\n26\t**Added method: `collect_prior_worker_artifacts`**\n27\t- Finds the most recent stopped worker (non-planner) in the run\n28\t- Returns their `produced_artifacts` array and `worker_id`\n29\t- Returns empty array and nil if no prior worker exists\n30\t- Called during `run_planner_turn` before publishing jobs\n31\t\n32\t**Modified method: `run_planner_turn`**\n33\t- Now calls `collect_prior_worker_artifacts` to get prior worker's artifacts\n34\t- Passes `prior_worker_artifacts` and `prior_worker_id` to `Planner.publish_planner_jobs`\n35\t- Maintains all existing behavior; addition is non-breaking\n36\t\n37\t### 2. Planner Module (app/services/orchestrator/planner.rb)\n38\t\n39\t**Updated method: `publish_planner_jobs`**\n40\t- Now accepts `prior_worker_artifacts` (default: []) parameter\n41\t- Now accepts `prior_worker_id` (default: nil) parameter\n42\t- Calls new `determine_inherited_artifacts` method to decide which artifacts to inherit\n43\t- Populates `inherited_artifacts` field in created SpawnRequest\n44\t- Populates `artifact_inheritance_chain` field with prior_worker_id for auditing\n45\t\n46\t**Added method: `determine_inherited_artifacts`**\n47\t- Current implementation: inherits all prior artifacts for any next step owner\n48\t- Future enhancement path: can be refined to selectively inherit based on step type (e.g., only diagnostic artifacts to verification steps)\n49\t- Accepts `prior_artifacts` (array) and `next_step_owner` (string, e.g., \"worker\", \"planner\")\n50\t\n51\t### 3. Database Schema\n52\t\n53\t**SpawnRequest table** (already existed, now used):\n54\t- `inherited_artifacts` (JSON array) — List of artifact names inherited from prior worker\n55\t- `artifact_inheritance_chain` (JSON array) — List of worker_ids in the inheritance chain for auditing\n56\t\n57\t**Worker table** (already existed, now updated):\n58\t- `produced_artifacts` (JSON array) — Updated by Turn.validate_and_record_artifacts! when worker reports completion\n59\t- Data populated via worker_turn MCP tool with `producedArtifacts` parameter\n60\t\n61\t---\n62\t\n63\t## Test Coverage\n64\t\n65\t### Phase 3 Artifact Inheritance Tests (new file: spec/services/orchestrator/phase_3_artifact_inheritance_spec.rb)\n66\t\n67\t**Test 1: Populates inherited_artifacts in SpawnRequest based on planner logic**\n68\t- Creates a prior worker with produced_artifacts: [\"diagnosis.md\", \"evidence.json\"]\n69\t- Planner creates new spawn request for next step\n70\t- Verifies inherited_artifacts contains both artifacts\n71\t- Verifies artifact_inheritance_chain includes prior_worker_id\n72\t\n73\t**Test 2: Handles diagnosis mode correctly**\n74\t- Creates prior worker with artifacts: [\"initial.md\", \"notes.txt\"]\n75\t- Planner creates diagnosis step\n76\t- Verifies artifacts are inherited regardless of step mode\n77\t- Verifies inheritance chain is recorded\n78\t\n79\t**Test 3: Handles runs with no prior worker gracefully**\n80\t- Creates planner decision with no prior worker in run\n81\t- Verifies inherited_artifacts is empty\n82\t- Verifies artifact_inheritance_chain is empty\n83\t- No errors or exceptions\n84\t\n85\t### Existing Tests (All Pass)\n86\t- 42 tests pass across:\n87\t  - planner_decision_job_spec.rb (6 tests)\n88\t  - planner_spec.rb (1 test)\n89\t  - planner_decision_submission_spec.rb (16 tests)\n90\t  - turn_spec.rb (4 tests)\n91\t  - spawn_requested_workers_spec.rb (12 tests)\n92\t  - phase_3_artifact_inheritance_spec.rb (3 tests)\n93\t\n94\t---\n95\t\n96\t## Backward Compatibility\n97\t\n98\t✓ All changes are backward compatible:\n99\t- New parameters have default values (empty arrays, nil)\n100\t- Existing spawn requests without inherited_artifacts continue to work\n101\t- Workers that don't declare produced_artifacts are unaffected\n102\t- No database migrations required (schema already supports fields)\n103\t\n104\t---\n105\t\n106\t## Architecture Flow\n107\t\n108\t```\n109\t1. Worker completes and calls worker_turn with producedArtifacts\n110\t   ↓\n111\t2. Turn.validate_and_record_artifacts! records them on Worker.produced_artifacts\n112\t   ↓\n113\t3. Turn.run_worker_turn creates planner SpawnRequest\n114\t   ↓\n115\t4. Planner decision submitted via PlannerDecisionSubmission.call\n116\t   ↓\n117\t5. Turn.run_planner_turn called with planner's next_step\n118\t   ↓\n119\t6. collect_prior_worker_artifacts finds most recent stopped worker\n120\t   ↓\n121\t7. Planner.publish_planner_jobs creates new SpawnRequest with:\n122\t   - inherited_artifacts: [prior worker's produced artifacts]\n123\t   - artifact_inheritance_chain: [prior_worker_id]\n124\t   ↓\n125\t8. New spawn request fulfills worker with inherited artifacts available\n126\t```\n127\t\n128\t---\n129\t\n130\t## Design Decisions\n131\t\n132\t1. **Inheritance is all-or-nothing** — Currently, all prior worker artifacts are inherited. This can be refined in future phases to be selective (e.g., only diagnostic artifacts for verification steps).\n133\t\n134\t2. **Inheritance chain is flat** — Only the immediate prior worker_id is recorded. Multi-generational lineage can be reconstructed from historical records if needed.\n135\t\n136\t3. **No validation at spawn time** — Inherited artifacts are not pre-validated to exist. The SpawnRequestedWorkers service can add optional validation before worker spawning if desired.\n137\t\n138\t4. **Graceful empty case** — If no prior worker exists (initial planner decision), inherited_artifacts is simply empty. No error or warning is generated.\n139\t\n140\t---\n141\t\n142\t## Code Quality\n143\t\n144\t- ✓ No comments added (code is self-documenting)\n145\t- ✓ No unnecessary abstractions (simple collection and inheritance)\n146\t- ✓ Follows existing patterns (Turn module already handles artifact validation)\n147\t- ✓ No error handling added (existing planner framework handles errors)\n148\t- ✓ All tests passing (no regressions)\n149\t\n150\t---\n151\t\n152\t## Future Enhancement Opportunities\n153\t\n154\t1. **Selective inheritance** — Refine `determine_inherited_artifacts` to consider step type:\n155\t   ```ruby\n156\t   case next_step_owner\n157\t   when \"verifier\" then filter_for_verification(artifacts)\n158\t   when \"infrastructure\" then filter_for_infrastructure(artifacts)\n159\t   else all_artifacts\n160\t   end\n161\t   ```\n162\t\n163\t2. **Artifact metadata in prompt** — Enhance `build_requested_worker_prompt` to include inherited artifact metadata (size, modification time, description).\n164\t\n165\t3. **Artifact discovery via collect_artifacts MCP tool** — Workers can query artifact metadata independently of prompt.\n166\t\n167\t4. **Mandatory artifact fields** — Support `required_artifacts` field on SpawnRequest to fail spawn if artifacts are missing.\n168\t\n169\t5. **Artifact retention policy** — Cleanup old artifacts after successful verification/completion based on age or run completion.\n170\t\n171\t---\n172\t\n173\t## Files Modified\n174\t\n175\t### Changed Files\n176\t- `app/services/orchestrator/turn.rb` (+18 lines)\n177\t  - Added `collect_prior_worker_artifacts` private method\n178\t  - Modified `run_planner_turn` to collect and pass prior artifacts\n179\t\n180\t- `app/services/orchestrator/planner.rb` (+23 lines)\n181\t  - Modified `publish_planner_jobs` to accept and populate inherited artifacts\n182\t  - Added `determine_inherited_artifacts` private method\n183\t\n184\t### New Files\n185\t- `spec/services/orchestrator/phase_3_artifact_inheritance_spec.rb` (+141 lines)\n186\t  - 3 comprehensive tests for Phase 3 functionality\n187\t\n188\t---\n189\t\n190\t## Evidence\n191\t\n192\tAll Phase 3 acceptance criteria confirmed:\n193\t\n194\t✓ **(1) Planner decision methods examine prior_worker.produced_artifacts**\n195\t- Turn.run_planner_turn calls collect_prior_worker_artifacts\n196\t- Prior worker is found via Worker.where(run_id, status: \"stopped\").order(stopped_at: :desc).first\n197\t- produced_artifacts is extracted and returned\n198\t\n199\t✓ **(2) SpawnRequests populated with inherited_artifacts based on planner logic**\n200\t- publish_planner_jobs receives prior_worker_artifacts parameter\n201\t- SpawnRequest created with inherited_artifacts field populated\n202\t- Test \"Populates inherited_artifacts in SpawnRequest\" confirms\n203\t\n204\t✓ **(3) Planner decisions include reasoning for artifact inheritance**\n205\t- artifact_inheritance_chain field records prior_worker_id\n206\t- RunContext entries track artifact production and inheritance\n207\t- Inheritance is auditable via database queries\n208\t\n209\t✓ **(4) All tests pass**\n210\t- 42 tests pass: 6 planner_decision_job + 1 planner + 16 planner_decision_submission + 4 turn + 12 spawn_requested_workers + 3 phase_3_artifact_inheritance\n211\t- No regressions detected\n212\t- All related specs confirmed passing\n213\t\n214\t---\n215\t\n216\t## Verification Commands\n217\t\n218\t```bash\n219\t# Run Phase 3 tests\n220\tbundle exec rspec spec/services/orchestrator/phase_3_artifact_inheritance_spec.rb\n221\t\n222\t# Run all affected test suites\n223\tbundle exec rspec spec/jobs/planner_decision_job_spec.rb spec/services/orchestrator/planner_spec.rb spec/services/orchestrator/planner_decision_submission_spec.rb spec/services/orchestrator/turn_spec.rb spec/services/orchestrator/spawn_requested_workers_spec.rb\n224\t\n225\t# Run full orchestrator suite (note: 3 pre-existing PTY failures unrelated to Phase 3)\n226\tbundle exec rspec spec/services/orchestrator/\n227\t```\n228\t\n229\t---\n230\t\n231\t## Next Steps\n232\t\n233\tPhase 3 is complete. The architecture now supports:\n234\t- Worker artifact declaration via `producedArtifacts` in worker_turn\n235\t- Planner-driven artifact inheritance via `inherited_artifacts` in spawn requests\n236\t- Full audit trail via `artifact_inheritance_chain`\n237\t\n238\tFor Phase 4 (future):\n239\t- Add `collect_artifacts` MCP tool for worker-driven discovery\n240\t- Extend `get_run_context` to return artifact metadata\n241\t- Add RunContext entries for artifact_inheritance_graph\n242\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25159a08-09b3-48ef-88b1-f3515df107c2","uuid":"d284d03d-3253-4f64-9ae9-95e4647398cc","timestamp":"2026-07-24T16:16:07.698Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/stockn/Source/workflow-orchestrator/when-launching-a-task-we-should-be-able-to-add-a-4780/front/demo-output/agents-sdk/run-20260724-120458-4780/phase-3-implementation.md","content":"# Phase 3 Implementation: Planner Artifact Inheritance\n\n**Status**: Complete ✓\n**Date**: 2026-07-24\n**Scope**: Implementation of planner decision methods to examine prior worker artifacts and populate inherited_artifacts in spawn requests.\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nPhase 3 successfully implements planner-side artifact inheritance. The planner now:\n\n1. **Examines prior worker produced_artifacts** — Collects artifacts from the most recent completed worker before creating new spawn requests\n2. **Populates inherited_artifacts in SpawnRequests** — Passes discovered artifacts to the next worker via the spawn request\n3. **Records artifact inheritance chain** — Maintains audit trail of which worker produced which artifacts\n4. **Includes reasoning for inheritance** — Artifact inheritance logic is traceable and auditable\n\nAll changes are backward compatible. Existing workflows without produced_artifacts declarations continue to work without modification.\n\n---\n\n## Changes Implemented\n\n### 1. Turn Module (app/services/orchestrator/turn.rb)\n\n**Added method: `collect_prior_worker_artifacts`**\n- Finds the most recent stopped worker (non-planner) in the run\n- Returns their `produced_artifacts` array and `worker_id`\n- Returns empty array and nil if no prior worker exists\n- Called during `run_planner_turn` before publishing jobs\n\n**Modified method: `run_planner_turn`**\n- Now calls `collect_prior_worker_artifacts` to get prior worker's artifacts\n- Passes `prior_worker_artifacts` and `prior_worker_id` to `Planner.publish_planner_jobs`\n- Maintains all existing behavior; addition is non-breaking\n\n### 2. Planner Module (app/services/orchestrator/planner.rb)\n\n**Updated method: `publish_planner_jobs`**\n- Now accepts `prior_worker_artifacts` (default: []) parameter\n- Now accepts `prior_worker_id` (default: nil) parameter\n- Calls new `determine_inherited_artifacts` method to decide which artifacts to inherit\n- Populates `inherited_artifacts` field in created SpawnRequest\n- Populates `artifact_inheritance_chain` field with prior_worker_id for auditing\n\n**Added method: `determine_inherited_artifacts`**\n- Current implementation: inherits all prior artifacts for any next step owner\n- Future enhancement path: can be refined to selectively inherit based on step type (e.g., only diagnostic artifacts to verification steps)\n- Accepts `prior_artifacts` (array) and `next_step_owner` (string, e.g., \"worker\", \"planner\")\n\n### 3. Database Schema\n\n**SpawnRequest table** (already existed, now used):\n- `inherited_artifacts` (JSON array) — List of artifact names inherited from prior worker\n- `artifact_inheritance_chain` (JSON array) — List of worker_ids in the inheritance chain for auditing\n\n**Worker table** (already existed, now updated):\n- `produced_artifacts` (JSON array) — Updated by Turn.validate_and_record_artifacts! when worker reports completion\n- Data populated via worker_turn MCP tool with `producedArtifacts` parameter\n\n---\n\n## Test Coverage\n\n### Phase 3 Artifact Inheritance Tests (new file: spec/services/orchestrator/phase_3_artifact_inheritance_spec.rb)\n\n**Test 1: Populates inherited_artifacts in SpawnRequest based on planner logic**\n- Creates a prior worker with produced_artifacts: [\"diagnosis.md\", \"evidence.json\"]\n- Planner creates new spawn request for next step\n- Verifies inherited_artifacts contains both artifacts\n- Verifies artifact_inheritance_chain includes prior_worker_id\n\n**Test 2: Handles diagnosis mode correctly**\n- Creates prior worker with artifacts: [\"initial.md\", \"notes.txt\"]\n- Planner creates diagnosis step\n- Verifies artifacts are inherited regardless of step mode\n- Verifies inheritance chain is recorded\n\n**Test 3: Handles runs with no prior worker gracefully**\n- Creates planner decision with no prior worker in run\n- Verifies inherited_artifacts is empty\n- Verifies artifact_inheritance_chain is empty\n- No errors or exceptions\n\n### Existing Tests (All Pass)\n- 42 tests pass across:\n  - planner_decision_job_spec.rb (6 tests)\n  - planner_spec.rb (1 test)\n  - planner_decision_submission_spec.rb (16 tests)\n  - turn_spec.rb (4 tests)\n  - spawn_requested_workers_spec.rb (12 tests)\n  - phase_3_artifact_inheritance_spec.rb (3 tests)\n\n---\n\n## Backward Compatibility\n\n✓ All changes are backward compatible:\n- New parameters have default values (empty arrays, nil)\n- Existing spawn requests without inherited_artifacts continue to work\n- Workers that don't declare produced_artifacts are unaffected\n- No database migrations required (schema already supports fields)\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Flow\n\n```\n1. Worker completes and calls worker_turn with producedArtifacts\n   ↓\n2. Turn.validate_and_record_artifacts! records them on Worker.produced_artifacts\n   ↓\n3. Turn.run_worker_turn creates planner SpawnRequest\n   ↓\n4. Planner decision submitted via PlannerDecisionSubmission.call\n   ↓\n5. Turn.run_planner_turn called with planner's next_step\n   ↓\n6. collect_prior_worker_artifacts finds most recent stopped worker\n   ↓\n7. Planner.publish_planner_jobs creates new SpawnRequest with:\n   - inherited_artifacts: [prior worker's produced artifacts]\n   - artifact_inheritance_chain: [prior_worker_id]\n   ↓\n8. New spawn request fulfills worker with inherited artifacts available\n```\n\n---\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n1. **Inheritance is all-or-nothing** — Currently, all prior worker artifacts are inherited. This can be refined in future phases to be selective (e.g., only diagnostic artifacts for verification steps).\n\n2. **Inheritance chain is flat** — Only the immediate prior worker_id is recorded. Multi-generational lineage can be reconstructed from historical records if needed.\n\n3. **No validation at spawn time** — Inherited artifacts are not pre-validated to exist. The SpawnRequestedWorkers service can add optional validation before worker spawning if desired.\n\n4. **Graceful empty case** — If no prior worker exists (initial planner decision), inherited_artifacts is simply empty. No error or warning is generated.\n\n---\n\n## Code Quality\n\n- ✓ No comments added (code is self-documenting)\n- ✓ No unnecessary abstractions (simple collection and inheritance)\n- ✓ Follows existing patterns (Turn module already handles artifact validation)\n- ✓ No error handling added (existing planner framework handles errors)\n- ✓ All tests passing (no regressions)\n\n---\n\n## Future Enhancement Opportunities\n\n1. **Selective inheritance** — Refine `determine_inherited_artifacts` to consider step type:\n   ```ruby\n   case next_step_owner\n   when \"verifier\" then filter_for_verification(artifacts)\n   when \"infrastructure\" then filter_for_infrastructure(artifacts)\n   else all_artifacts\n   end\n   ```\n\n2. **Artifact metadata in prompt** — Enhance `build_requested_worker_prompt` to include inherited artifact metadata (size, modification time, description).\n\n3. **Artifact discovery via collect_artifacts MCP tool** — Workers can query artifact metadata independently of prompt.\n\n4. **Mandatory artifact fields** — Support `required_artifacts` field on SpawnRequest to fail spawn if artifacts are missing.\n\n5. **Artifact retention policy** — Cleanup old artifacts after successful verification/completion based on age or run completion.\n\n---\n\n## Files Modified\n\n### Changed Files\n- `app/services/orchestrator/turn.rb` (+18 lines)\n  - Added `collect_prior_worker_artifacts` private method\n  - Modified `run_planner_turn` to collect and pass prior artifacts\n\n- `app/services/orchestrator/planner.rb` (+23 lines)\n  - Modified `publish_planner_jobs` to accept and populate inherited artifacts\n  - Added `determine_inherited_artifacts` private method\n\n### New Files\n- `spec/services/orchestrator/phase_3_artifact_inheritance_spec.rb` (+141 lines)\n  - 3 comprehensive tests for Phase 3 functionality\n\n---\n\n## Evidence\n\nAll Phase 3 acceptance criteria confirmed:\n\n✓ **(1) Planner decision methods examine prior_worker.produced_artifacts**\n- Turn.run_planner_turn calls collect_prior_worker_artifacts\n- Prior worker is found via Worker.where(run_id, status: \"stopped\").order(stopped_at: :desc).first\n- produced_artifacts is extracted and returned\n\n✓ **(2) SpawnRequests populated with inherited_artifacts based on planner logic**\n- publish_planner_jobs receives prior_worker_artifacts parameter\n- SpawnRequest created with inherited_artifacts field populated\n- Test \"Populates inherited_artifacts in SpawnRequest\" confirms\n\n✓ **(3) Planner decisions include reasoning for artifact inheritance**\n- artifact_inheritance_chain field records prior_worker_id\n- RunContext entries track artifact production and inheritance\n- Inheritance is auditable via database queries\n\n✓ **(4) All tests pass**\n- 42 tests pass: 6 planner_decision_job + 1 planner + 16 planner_decision_submission + 4 turn + 12 spawn_requested_workers + 3 phase_3_artifact_inheritance\n- No regressions detected\n- All related specs confirmed passing\n\n---\n\n## Verification Commands\n\n```bash\n# Run Phase 3 tests\nbundle exec rspec spec/services/orchestrator/phase_3_artifact_inheritance_spec.rb\n\n# Run all affected test suites\nbundle exec rspec spec/jobs/planner_decision_job_spec.rb spec/services/orchestrator/planner_spec.rb spec/services/orchestrator/planner_decision_submission_spec.rb spec/services/orchestrator/turn_spec.rb spec/services/orchestrator/spawn_requested_workers_spec.rb\n\n# Run full orchestrator suite (note: 3 pre-existing PTY failures unrelated to Phase 3)\nbundle exec rspec spec/services/orchestrator/\n```\n\n---\n\n## Next Steps\n\nPhase 3 is complete. The architecture now supports:\n- Worker artifact declaration via `producedArtifacts` in worker_turn\n- Planner-driven artifact inheritance via `inherited_artifacts` in spawn requests\n- Full audit trail via `artifact_inheritance_chain`\n\nFor Phase 4 (future):\n- Add `collect_artifacts` MCP tool for worker-driven discovery\n- Extend `get_run_context` to return artifact metadata\n- Add RunContext entries for artifact_inheritance_graph\n","numLines":242,"startLine":1,"totalLines":242}}}
